From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Batocera Team <batocera-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Oct 2024 11:55:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Read the CPU temperature from cpu0_thermal on the Batocera
 RPMini

On the Qualcomm SM8250 (Batocera RPMini) the CPU temperature sensor is
called cpu0_thermal; look for it in the thermal zones.

Taken from batocera.linux, package/batocera/utils/mangohud/003-add-sm8250.patch
(LGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright The Batocera Team).

diff --git a/src/cpu.cpp b/src/cpu.cpp
index f46fabad1a7b461e2064170016b57baef2e605dc..2e9771059b80dd1b2025ddd88f29fd8b2eb1911f 100644
--- a/src/cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/cpu.cpp
@@ -615,6 +615,10 @@ bool CPUStats::GetCpuFile() {
         } else if (name == "apm_xgene") {
             find_input(path, "temp", input, "SoC Temperature");
             break;
+        } else if (name == "cpu0_thermal") { // Batocera RPMini sm8250
+            find_input(path, "temp", input, "temp1");
+            break;
+
         } else {
             path.clear();
         }
